{"kind":"event","event_id":5557,"event_uid":"01M2MCBTZWFAXPZET97NV2KXSK","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":255,"issue_uid":"01M2MC5W0AXZEPK5704H8J9ZTC","issue_short_id":"9ztc","actor":"impl:1@run-155","hlc_physical_ms":1789537938428,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"adbe8c44bc33d1978a304a3d6ddae95c81bd7a59028951e105ef81ada8101d30","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCBTZVGZJKY564Y7K7W7NF","author":"impl:1@run-155","body":"Landed both halves. fleet/roles/implementer.md gains '## The state you reached' directly after '## The issue': the key state.reached, the one command `kata meta set $KATA_REF state.reached \"{...}\" --json-value` with the path as a placeholder, the two fields expected (path under state-exams/expected/) and content (the getContent() pair), and the three rules — after the task's own exam is green, 'post it once', and 'only a task whose Proof names a state exam'. Decision worth recording: the --json-value flag is named in prose AFTER the command block, because leg (a)'s regex wants --json-value before 'expected' and 'content' while the command string spells the fields first.\n\nfleet/CONTRACT.md: one paragraph appended to the KATA_REF paragraph of the 'Kata record (engine)' bullet (not at the bullet's end, to stay clear of Task 2's likely append on the same file), naming state.reached, expected, content, the producing task's implementer as sole poster and the driver as sole reader, in that order. It deliberately does not spell Task 2's engine-side mechanics (the hub request, state-exams/posted/, the fact:state.reached event) — that is Task 2's to write in the same bullet.\n\nAll six proof legs green; test_sims_are_hermetic plus the seven other sims touching role files also pass.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:52:18.427861742Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:52:18.428Z"}
