{"kind":"event","event_id":5572,"event_uid":"01M2MCK605HTB4BWKVZQNBQ26M","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":256,"issue_uid":"01M2MC5ZMFHQ8VVVCRRT7R293P","issue_short_id":"293p","actor":"impl:2@run-155","hlc_physical_ms":1789538179077,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"f58d420f5f71cceae862cc4982aaa69cb230cd74fc7587d0b50b69bdad523c2a","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCK603KVGRMVHQZHFEKJTE","author":"impl:2@run-155","body":"Task 2 approach: (1) module-level in fleet/run-engine.mjs — export `handshakeOf(issue)` (well-formed post or null), plus `handshakeFault`, canonical-JSON sha256 and the first-differing-cell renderer, dropped in after `stateExamBlock`. (2) M1 — per-task seeding in runTaskInner: producers come off the run's dependency edges (`predecessorsOf`, falling back to the `a -> b` strings), one fresh `kataCall('getissue')` per producer (the Setup read predates the post, so it cannot carry it), `content` written compact to `state-exams/posted/<producer>.json` in both the task clone and the examiner's, seeded at the end of `cutExamClone` and again for the graded clone before the pair is dispatched — i.e. before any exam command of the task runs. The seed path is added to each clone's `.git/info/exclude` so `git add -A` never folds run-local state into the target. (3) M2 — a `handshakeCheck()` at the tail of `prePass()`: reads the task's own issue, compares the parsed `expected` file in the graded clone with `content`, appends `handshake:settled` when equal and otherwise pushes one red whose line is the `handshake:` finding, which is what buys the `fix:<id>:0` round. (4) findings are recorded per task and surface as a new `tasks[].findings` key on the report row (`{severity, actor, detail}`), deduped by detail, beside one `handshake:finding` event. (5) `fact:state.reached {task, expected, sha256}` is appended once per post (deduped by task+sha256), so a post read at both M1 and M2 is one event. Everything is gated on `kataOn`, and no prompt-building code is touched.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:56:19.075792110Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:56:19.077Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5598,"event_uid":"01M2MCMQEHWWHVX7NPZQR52Y0B","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":256,"issue_uid":"01M2MC5ZMFHQ8VVVCRRT7R293P","issue_short_id":"293p","actor":"exam:2@run-155","hlc_physical_ms":1789538229713,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"af04760a47306c38d7d3387c1647049a4ed8be524b8b4236848e470abaf330c9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCMQEGKQ8CA7T05A1JG4GF","author":"exam:2@run-155","body":"examiner (task 2, the state handshake): approach before the long stretch.\n\nThe exam lands at `fleet/tests/exams/run_155/test_run_engine_state_handshake.mjs` (EXAM PATHS), so every relative import is written for that depth — `../../../run-engine.mjs` is the engine, `../../_engine_helpers.mjs` the rig.\n\nShape: one engine sim per leg, on the same two-task plan — producer `1`, consumer `2`, edge `1 -> 2` (the consumer's `Consumes:` edge the compiler emits), a fake hub of the `makeFakeKata` shape copied from `test_worker_kata_env.mjs`/`test_run_engine_kata_landing.mjs`, and a stub worker seam. The consumer's Proof path is a shell exam the examiner stub writes into its own clone; its command records what it can read of `state-exams/posted/1.json` into a witness directory under `$ULTRA_RUN_DIR`, at both passes the driver runs it (`base` in `clones/exam-2`, `0` in `clones/task-2`) — that is leg (a)'s 'measured by an exam command that reads the file', and it is how 'before the exam command first runs' is read as a fact about the moment rather than about the tree afterwards.\n\nThree readings I am writing the file on, recorded here because a later session would otherwise have to reconstruct them:\n\n1. The post is written by the producer's IMPLEMENTER, during its session (the global constraint says so), so the stub writes `state.reached` into the fake's store as the `impl:1` session ends — not into the issue at setup. The driver's Setup-time `getIssue` (`openKataTask`) therefore cannot be the read M1/M2 name; the handshake needs a read of its own. That write does not bump the fake's revision, exactly as the attention-hook's write does not in the landing sim.\n2. M3's 'every post the driver reads under M1 or M2 is appended once' is read as once per POST, not once per read: in the leg (a)/(c) run the same post is read twice (the consumer's seed, the producer's pre-review compare) and the exam asserts EXACTLY ONE `fact:state.reached`.\n3. M2's detail names 'the first differing cell'. The fixtures differ in exactly ONE cell, so the cell named is the same under any traversal order — the exam pins the detail string, not an iteration order the clause never fixes. That cell's value is a boolean, so `true`/`false` renders the same under `String` and `JSON.stringify` and the detail is unambiguous.\n\nLeg (h)'s 'byte-identical to the prompt the same run produces at BASE' is measured by importing the BASE engine out of a `git worktree` cut at  and running the same plan through it, in the same run-directory path (the first run's tree is removed and re-provisioned) so the patch paths the reviewer prompt carries are identical by construction; both engines are handed the same `rolesDir`, so a sibling's role-file edit cannot move the comparison.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:09.712343943Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:09.713Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5714,"event_uid":"01M2MDCQXN210CB94Y09QTNR6M","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":256,"issue_uid":"01M2MC5ZMFHQ8VVVCRRT7R293P","issue_short_id":"293p","actor":"exam:2@run-155","hlc_physical_ms":1789539016629,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"526d05dc111760c541d620187eac5342c6a470826fedd1dc47df989614c247ad","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MDCQXKKZPJEBHDQJ4F9PQS","author":"exam:2@run-155","body":"Exam landed at fleet/tests/exams/run_155/test_run_engine_state_handshake.mjs (nothing at the Proof path). Red at BASE for one reason: run-engine.mjs exports no `handshakeOf`, so the named import does not link.\n\nHow I checked it is red only for that reason: a throwaway copy with a local `handshakeOf` and a soft `assert` ran all nine sim runs end to end — 36 assertion failures, every one of them a handshake claim, and not a single `sim precondition` assertion among them. So the rig itself is green at BASE; only the feature is missing. 5.5s wall clock.\n\nFour readings a later session would otherwise have to reconstruct:\n\n1. The post is written mid-session by the PRODUCER'S IMPLEMENTER (the run's constraint says so: `kata meta set state.reached --json-value` on its own issue). The fake hub's `post()` sets the metadata without recording a call and without bumping the revision — so the driver's Setup-time `getIssue` in `openKataTask` cannot be the read M1/M2 name, and a fresh read is forced. Same trick the landing sim uses for the attention hook's SessionEnd write.\n\n2. M3's \"appended once\" is read as once per POST, not once per READ. Run A reads the same post twice — to seed the consumer under M1, to compare under M2 — and the exam asserts EXACTLY ONE `fact:state.reached`.\n\n3. M2's \"first differing cell\": the fixture differs in exactly ONE cell, so no traversal order is pinned. That cell holds a boolean (`todos/0/completed`, posted true / file false) so the detail has one spelling under `String` and under `JSON.stringify`: `handshake: todos/0/completed got true wanted false`.\n\n4. `blocking` + `actor: implementer` are asserted through the routing the clause itself defines (\"routed to `fix:<id>:0` exactly as any blocking finding\"), because the engine keeps no per-task findings array a sim can read. So: exactly one `- handshake: ...` line in the `fix:1:0` prompt's blocking block, the same one line in the `review round 0:` comment the driver posts on the producer's issue, the same in the failed row's notes, the row `failed` with no referee dispatched — and, for `implementer` and not `plan`, no `plan-defect` entry in `deferredVerification` and no `actor: plan` on the row.\n\nTwo more mechanics worth knowing:\n- Leg (a)'s \"measured by an exam command that reads the file\" is a real shell Proof the examiner stub writes; its command copies `state-exams/posted/1.json` into `$ULTRA_RUN_DIR/witness/<task>-<pass>/` at both passes (`base` in clones/exam-2, `0` in clones/task-2), and records `pwd` so the exam proves which clone each pass ran in. It always exits 0, so a missing seed is recorded rather than turned into a red that would reshape the run.\n- Leg (h) imports the BASE engine out of `git archive 901fc874` into a temp tree and runs the same plan through it, same repo, same runDir PATH (so patch paths in the reviewer prompt match by construction), with both engines handed the same temp `rolesDir` (no role file of the checkout — one of which task 1 is editing — can move the comparison). `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE`/`GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` are pinned for the process, without which wave 2's BASE is a timestamped fold sha and three prompts differ. Verified: 0 byte diffs across all five prompt files.\n\nLeg (i) is read as \"the client is handed over but the record is not\" — that is what `--kata` absent means to the engine (`kataOn` needs both halves), and it is the only way to COUNT zero `getIssue` rather than merely not observe one. That leg is necessarily green at BASE; M4 says as much (\"behaves exactly as at BASE\").\n\nNothing unsatisfiable. All nine legs plus a direct unit block on `handshakeOf` itself (M5's well-formedness, both malformed halves, and the fact that a third key does not make a value malformed).","created_at":"2026-09-16T06:10:16.628000419Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T06:10:16.629Z"}
